X("mdma","MDMA (ecstasy, molly)","emp","Ring-substituted amphetamine; serotonin, dopamine and noradrenaline releaser.","Ecstasy, E, X, molly, mandy, XTC, beans.",
"Merck patented MDMA in 1912 as an intermediate chemical. Alexander Shulgin resynthesized it in 1976 and introduced it to therapist Leo Zeff, who shared it with hundreds of therapists. Club use spread in the 1980s (rave culture); the DEA emergency-scheduled it in 1985. MAPS-sponsored trials for PTSD led to an FDA application that the FDA declined in 2024, requesting another study.",
"Investigated for MDMA-assisted therapy for PTSD; Australia allowed psychiatrist prescribing in 2023.","Popular at clubs, raves and festivals; many 'molly' samples contain cathinones or other drugs.","US Schedule I; UN 1971 Schedule I.",
["MDMA's character is emotional openness and warmth: deep empathy, a sense of connection, talkativeness, and pleasure in touch and music.","Body effects include jaw clenching, teeth grinding, sweating, eye wiggles and raised temperature.","The comedown and the days after ('Tuesday blues') bring low mood as serotonin is depleted. Deaths result mainly from overheating, low blood sodium and drug interactions."],
["Swallowed, effects begin 30 to 60 minutes later, often with nausea and a rush of anxiety.","A wave of warmth and energy builds.","The peak at 1.5 to 2.5 hours brings maximal euphoria and empathy.","Plateau about 1 to 2 hours.","Comedown over 2 hours with fatigue.","Low mood and jaw ache.","Low mood for days in some people."],
{"oral":t("30-60 min","1-1.5 h","1.5-2.5 h","2-4 h","4-6 h","6-24 h","2-4 days")},{"oral":"Pills, capsules or crystals."},
"MDMA deaths are mostly from overheating, low blood sodium (from drinking too much water plus MDMA's hormone effects), serotonin syndrome and heart problems.",
"Ecstasy pills come in many colors and logos, which say nothing about content; molly is usually off-white crystals or capsules. High-strength pills are common in Europe."+CW,
"MDMA is metabolized by CYP2D6, and it blocks that enzyme as it goes, so levels can rise disproportionately with redosing.",
ext=("MDMA is absorbed from the gut and reverses the serotonin transporter, flooding synapses with serotonin; it also releases dopamine and noradrenaline.","Heart rate, blood pressure and body temperature begin to rise; pupils dilate.","At peak, MDMA triggers release of oxytocin and vasopressin (antidiuretic hormone); vasopressin makes the kidneys hold water, so drinking large amounts of water can dangerously dilute blood sodium, causing brain swelling.","Overheating is worsened by hot crowded venues and dancing; serotonin syndrome is more likely with antidepressants, tramadol, DXM, MAOIs and other serotonergic drugs.","MDMA's half-life is about 7 to 9 hours; because it inhibits CYP2D6, redosing raises levels more than expected.","Serotonin depletion explains low mood for days afterward; heavy repeated use is linked to memory problems."),
src=S+["Passie T. The early use of MDMA in psychotherapy. Drug Science, Policy and Law 2018","FDA complete response letter on midomafetamine (2024)"])
